.SH NAME
AR860 - Creates and maintains archives for the iPSC\*R/860\fR\fR\fR\fR\& system.
.\" End Summary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
\&\fBar860\fR\fR\& [ \fB\&-q\fR\fR\& ] \fR\fIkey\fI\fR\& [ \fR\fI\
options\fI\fR\& ] \fR\fIlibname\fI\fR\& [ \fR\fIfilename\fI\fR\
\& ...] 
.SH ARGUMENTS 
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fR\fIlibname\fI\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' The name of the archive. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fR\fIfilename\fI\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' The name of the target file. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fB\&-q\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Do not display the tool banner (tool name, version, etc.).
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.LP
You must specify one, and only one, \fR\fIkey\fI\fR\& from the following list:
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fBr\fR\fR\&[\fBu\fR\fR\&] 	\h'-\w' 'u' Replace the file \fR\fI\
filename\fI\fR\& in the archive \fR\fIlibname\fI\fR\&. If the optional \fB\
u\fR\fR\& is specified, then \&``update'' the archive (i.e., replace the archive version only if \fR\fI\
filename\fI\fR\& is newer). If \fR\fIlibname\fI\fR\& does not exist, then create it (unless \fB\
\&-c\fR\fR\& \fR\fIoption\fI\fR\& is specified). If \fR\fIfilename\fI\fR\
\& does not appear in the archive, then add it. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fBd\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Delete \fR\fIfilename\fI\fR\& from the archive.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fBt\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Display the archive table of contents.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fBe\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Display the symbol tables of COFF objects in the archive.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fBp\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Display the archive version of \fR\fI\
filename\fI\fR\&.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fBx\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Extract \fR\fIfilename\fI\fR\& from the archive. If no file is named, extract all files.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.LP
You may specify the following \fR\fIoptions\fI\fR\& in any order:
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fBc\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' If \fR\fIlibname\fI\fR\& does not already exist, do not create it (overrides \fB\
\&-r\fR\fR\& \fR\fIkey\fI\fR\&).
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fBl\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Use the current working directory for temporary files.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fBv\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Verbose mode. For \fB\&-r\fR\fR\&, display the names of the archive members as they are \
replaced (or added). For \fB\&-d\fR\fR\&, display the names of the archive members as they are \
deleted. For \fB\&-t\fR\fR\&, display the file mode, the \fR\fI\
uid\fI\fR\&, the \fR\fIgid\fI\fR\&, the size, and the timestamp \
of the specified files. For \fB\&-x\fR\fR\&, display the names of the files as they are extracted. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.0i 5.9i
.HP 1i
\fBa\fR\fR\&, \fBb\fR\fR\&, \fBi\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Do nothing. Accepted for compatibility.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
Use\fB\& ar860\fR\fR\& to manage archives for the iPSC/860\& system. 
.LP
The dash prefix is required only for the \fB\&-q\fR\fR\& argument, but current convention recommends using it \
for all arguments (\fR\fIkey\fI\fR\& and \fR\fIoptions\fI\fR\&).
.SH SEE ALSO
.LP
\fBas860\fR\fR\&, \fBdump860\fR\fR\&, \fBicc\fR\fR\&, \fBif77\fR\fR\
\&, \fBld860\fR\fR\&, \fBnm860\fR\fR\&, \fBsize860\fR\fR\&, \fB\
strip860\fR\fR\& 
.LP
\fR\fR
.LP
.LP
